VALUES (591, '0', $t$ASK 591: the judge order is a table the operator sets from the dashboard (with fix 1 and fix 2)$t$,
  $t$The operator can order the judges and the alternates himself, on a dashboard page, and the engine seats from that order. Before, the order stood as fixed arrays in the engine code (Init Seats ORDER0 and __ALT, Accept Build ORDER), so a change of order needed an engine build. (Plan ask591/w3/plan591.md; the operator asked at 23:23 CST 2026-11-23 and again at 00:41 CST 2026-11-24, and pressed "Build it" at 00:46 CST 2026-11-24, ruling row 517.)$t$,
  'in part',
  $t$Three writes by W4, each on the operator's press in W4's thread as the Wall and the audit rows give them. (1) ASK 591, press "Write all three", written 08:51 CST 2026-11-24 (Wall 11543; audit 41446). Database (mig591.sql adbadc73): tables odv1_judge_order (seeded from the live order: panel chatgpt, sol, sol62; alternates gemini, spark, qwen4max, argon, sonnet) and odv1_judge_order_log (version 1); functions odv1_judge_order_lists, _fault, _read, _save, dash_judge_order, dash_judge_lineup; three dash_api actions (dash_api 9888582a to a866c092). Engine 489b977b to 347f3e21, 422 to 423 nodes, child untouched: new node Judge Order Read between each start path and Accept Models; Accept Build ORDER, Init Seats ORDER0 and __ALT come from the read; Init Seats' output gains judge_order; Build Save Body adds one review_notes line "[JUDGE ORDER v<n>: ...]"; a missing or bad read stops the run with no fallback order. Dashboard: new tab "Judge order" (judge591.js), patch.js loads it, odv1.js loses haiku from its static list. W1 readback: engine MATCH, database MATCH, dashboard files MATCH (Wall 11544, 11547). (2) Fix 1, press "Write the fix", written 09:21 CST (Wall 11556; audit 41463), after the operator's words of 09:18 CST as Wall 11554 gives them: "i see single judge ... we don't have single judge anymore". Engine 137378eb to 6834c21b: Build Save Body's review line loses "; single judge <seat>". Database: dash_judge_lineup f704ad29 to caea9e6c, no single judge computed or returned. Dashboard: the "Single judge" row deleted (judge591.js sha1 b00c6868). W1 readback MATCH (Wall 11557). (3) Fix 2, press "Write it now", written 09:34 CST (Wall 11559; audit 41468): the operator's Save on the page failed with "requires a WHERE clause" (21000), because odv1_judge_order_save cleared the table with a bare DELETE and the dashboard's database role runs with the safeupdate guard; the save rolled back whole (version stayed 1, 8 rows). One line changed: the clearing ends WHERE true (definition f0dae4d1 to 47b637c5). W1 readback MATCH (Wall 11561). MISTAKES in the record: W4 called the page live before the production alias pointed to the new deployment (W1 found it, Wall 11544 F4; W4 moved the alias, Wall 11546). W4's and W1's tests of the save ran without the safeupdate guard, so neither saw the bare DELETE (Wall 11559, 11561). The first build showed a single judge on the page and in the review line although the single judge is switched off (ruling 402); the operator found it. Fix 2 was written with W1's grade PASS ON READING, TEST NOT RUN, because the approval prompt could not reach the operator and he chose to write. Deviations from the plan, both stated and accepted by W1 (Wall 11540, 11542): the panel list needs at least three seats, not four; the save refuses any seat that is not on the reserve recorder's list, where the plan said to warn. IN PART, because no run has executed since the writes (debate_results last row 21:57 CST 2026-11-23), so no run has read the order from the table. The save from the page is shown: after fix 2 the operator saved at 09:43 CST 2026-11-24 (odv1_judge_order_log row 2, saved_by dashboard; the table now holds panel sol, sol62, spark and alternates chatgpt, qwen4max, gemini, argon, sonnet; read by W3 by SQL and by W1, Wall 11572). Left for ASK 598 (W1's F1, Wall 11555): three single-judge texts in Build Save Body and Init Seats' single_judge field. RUN REVISION (this row; where a sentence above says that no run has executed or that a path is unexercised, this paragraph is the later word): run ODV1-42373-tg0w4edj (debate_results e7f6922f, row created 17:21 CST 2026-11-24; engine 20db58ee, child 74353c40; anthropic/claude-opus-5.5 as the Oracle defending against anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; outcome UNDERDETERMINED, panel BROKEN 2-1). The engine read the order from the table: the run's judge order line carries version 5 of the table, names no single judge, and the first alternate of the SEATED list was the one seated. W3 counts this as the first of the two live runs with no issue that the operator's rule asks, for ASK 591 at order version 5 (agreed by W1, Wall 11785); IN PART until the second (W1, Wall 11890). LIMIT: whether Judge Order Read executed before Accept Models is in the execution only. Run 42283 carried the line at version 2 and ended in error at the judges' call. In this run no panel send-back was sent (53 of 58 rows read "NOT SENT: no panel request for this seat"; the cause is the ASK 611 build, since fixed by fix 2 and not shown by a run), so nothing that needs a panel send-back was shown. The operator's rule of 10:38 CST 2026-11-24 asks two live runs with no issues; status stays 'read back'.$t$,
  '11413, 11419, 11543, 11556, 11559, 11872, 11875, 11890',
